---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Default.astro';
import site from '../../data/config.json';
import apps from '../../data/staff_apps.json';
const guides = apps.filter((app) => app.record_url);
---
<Layout title="The Future of Community Marketing" description="Why community marketing is moving into places communities own, and how AudienceKit's contextual, flat-priced advertising pays for the community instead of mining it. Download the pitch deck and document.">

<section class="section wrap scene sov-hero" aria-labelledby="pitch-title">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">AudienceKit · The pitch</p>
    <h1 id="pitch-title">The future of<br>community <em>marketing.</em></h1>
  </div>
  <div class="scene-copy">
    <p class="large-copy">We host communities. We don’t collect people.</p>
    <p>Community marketing is moving off rented platforms and into places communities own. Each community gets its own app, its members stay its own, and businesses reach it through placements priced flat on a public rate card and matched to the city, the night and the event, never to a profile of the person looking. The revenue goes back toward the cost of running the community.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section capabilities" id="live" aria-labelledby="live-title" hidden data-stats-url="https://api.audiencekit.com/v1/public/audiences/hotmess/stats">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Live from Hot Mess</p>
      <h2 class="capability-title" id="live-title"><span data-stat="venues"></span> venues in <span data-stat="places"></span> places</h2>
      <p class="capability-intro">Counted from the platform as you read this, not typed into a slide. Hot Mess is in the App Store and Google Play in the US; its listings reach further. <span data-stat="as_of"></span></p>
    </div>
    <div class="capability-grid" data-stat="countries"></div>
  </div>
</section>

<script is:inline>
(() => {
  const section = document.getElementById('live');
  if (!section) return;
  const fmt = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US');
  fetch(section.dataset.statsUrl, { headers: { Accept: 'application/json' } })
    .then((r) => (r.ok ? r.json() : Promise.reject(r.status)))
    .then((stats) => {
      if (!stats || !stats.venues || !Array.isArray(stats.countries)) return;
      const set = (key, text) => section.querySelectorAll(`[data-stat="${key}"]`).forEach((el) => { el.textContent = text; });
      set('venues', fmt.format(stats.venues));
      set('places', fmt.format(stats.places));
      if (stats.as_of) {
        const when = new Date(stats.as_of);
        if (!Number.isNaN(when.getTime())) set('as_of', `Updated ${when.toLocaleString('en-US', { dateStyle: 'medium', timeStyle: 'short' })}.`);
      }
      const grid = section.querySelector('[data-stat="countries"]');
      stats.countries.slice().sort((a, b) => b.venues - a.venues).forEach((c) => {
        const card = document.createElement('article');
        card.className = 'capability-card';
        const h = document.createElement('h3');
        h.textContent = c.name || c.code;
        const p = document.createElement('p');
        p.textContent = `${fmt.format(c.venues)} venues in ${fmt.format(c.places)} ${c.places === 1 ? 'place' : 'places'}`;
        card.append(h, p);
        grid.append(card);
      });
      section.hidden = false;
    })
    .catch(() => {});
})();
</script>

<section class="section capabilities" id="downloads" aria-labelledby="downloads-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Downloads</p>
      <h2 class="capability-title" id="downloads-title">Read it your way</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="capability-grid">
      <article class="capability-card">
        <h3>Pitch deck</h3>
        <p>Sixteen slides: what broke on the big platforms, the AudienceKit model, our six advertising rules, the sample ads running in AudienceKit Demo, the four advertising levels (none, sponsorship only, privacy-protected or traditional) and how publisher ads stay separate, the hybrid SDK model, Soapbox and the local press, safety, Velvet’s one-tap safety alerts and proof.</p>
        <p><a class="text-link" href="/pitch/future-of-community-marketing-deck.pdf">Download the deck (PDF, 0.8 MB) <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></p>
      </article>
      <article class="capability-card">
        <h3>Pitch document</h3>
        <p>The full argument in eleven pages, with the rules every placement follows, the nine sample cards in AudienceKit Demo, the four advertising levels, the hybrid model and its trade-off, the marketing surfaces in the apps, how Soapbox brings publishers in without cutting out curators, how Velvet safety alerts get staff to a guest, and who AudienceKit is for.</p>
        <p><a class="text-link" href="/pitch/future-of-community-marketing.pdf">Download the document (PDF, 0.6 MB) <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section capabilities" id="walkthroughs" aria-labelledby="walkthroughs-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">The apps, step by step</p>
      <h2 class="capability-title" id="walkthroughs-title">Walk through the apps</h2>
      <p class="capability-intro">Screen-by-screen guides to the AudienceKit apps that organizers, venues and performers use every night.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="capability-grid">
      {guides.map((app) => (
        <article class="capability-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">{app.role}</p>
          <h3>{app.name}</h3>
          <p>{app.summary}</p>
          <p><a class="text-link" href={app.record_url}>{app.record_label} <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></p>
          <p><a class="text-link" href={`/apps/${app.slug}/`}>Get {app.name} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section wrap closing" aria-labelledby="pitch-closing-title"><p class="eyebrow">You bring the people.</p><h2 id="pitch-closing-title">Let’s make<br><em>your scene.</em></h2><p>Tell us about the community you’re building.<br>We’ll help you bring it into focus.</p><a class="button primary" href={`mailto:${site.contact_email}?subject=Make%20a%20Scene`}>Start a conversation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>

</Layout>
